  "scopeNote" : {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Protein exotoxins from Staphylococcus aureus, phage type II, which cause epidermal necrolysis. They are proteins with a molecular weight of 26,000 to 32,000. They cause a condition variously called scaled skin, Lyell or Ritter syndrome, epidermal exfoliative disease, toxic epidermal necrolysis, etc."
  },
  "term" : [ "http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/T015557", "http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/T015559" ],
